# Epic close — **SWAT** (permission **and** the SWAT work)

**Do not run SWAT** (review swarm, epic status close, GitHub Release) until **both:**

1. **SWAT work is the job this turn** — code-reviewer, dead-code, tech-debt, security if relevant, merge-ready. List: [wrap-on-command.mdc](wrap-on-command.mdc).
2. **Permission this conversation** — they typed **SWAT**, **or** this **CMPH** is the epic’s last in-scope story (that CMPH includes SWAT).

A mid-epic CMPH is **not** SWAT permission. Do not start the swarm because the epic “looks done.”

Mid-epic **CMPH** does **not** run this swarm.

## Quality gates (required — SWAT)

Run [.cursor/rules/handoff-checklist.mdc](handoff-checklist.mdc) → *SWAT / epic close only*:

1. Code review (code-reviewer)
2. Dead code (dead-code-remover)
3. Tech debt evaluation (tech-debt-evaluator) → update `TECH_DEBT.md` as needed
4. Tests / coverage (merge-ready command from `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` / `TEST_PLAN.md`)
5. Project readiness (optional / N/A)
6. Security review when relevant (security-reviewer)
7. Tier 2 when the epic’s behavior requires it

Do **not** treat epic close as docs-only and skip review, debt, or tests.

## Then status close

Follow [.cursor/skills/pm-governance/SKILL.md](../skills/pm-governance/SKILL.md) → *Epic close*: mark the epic/phase complete in `PM_PLAN` / product plan, sync `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` + `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` → *Current state*, write the close/handoff note, commit/push the **feature branch**. Merge to `main` only after the user approves ([no-auto-merge-main.mdc](no-auto-merge-main.mdc)). **After merge to `main`:** cut a **GitHub Release** (tag `v{info.json}`, attach `dist/*.zip`, player notes) — do not wait to be asked. **Nexus Mods:** do not upload until the mod is playable; then help with the page. See [docs/Versioning_and_Release_Strategy.md](../../docs/Versioning_and_Release_Strategy.md).

## Do not auto-do on close

- Start the next epic’s implementation unless the user already asked or **Next** already directed it.
- Retire prototypes / dual trees or other deferred debt unless the user or plan **Next** says so this session.
- Re-open explicitly cut features.
